pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
f 1;
% Lowering the RHS of a literal axiom and then adding it must contribute the
% lowered degree. The literal-axiom stash used to swallow the "3 -" here,
% deriving 1 x1 2 x2 >= 1 instead of >= -2 (sound, but not the constraint
% this derivation states). Found by the proved-kernel shadow replay.
pol 1 x2 3 - +;
e 1 x1 2 x2 >= -2 : 2;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
